---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { embedded, type Row } from "../data/bench";

const fmt = (n: number) => n.toLocaleString("en-US");
const ratio = (r: Row) => r.dengine / r.etcd;

const hello = `use d_engine::prelude::*;
use std::time::Duration;

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() {
    let engine = DefaultEmbeddedEngine::start("./data").await.unwrap();
    engine.wait_ready(Duration::from_secs(5)).await.unwrap();

    let client = engine.client();
    client.put(b"hello".to_vec(), b"world".to_vec()).await.unwrap();
    let value = client.get_linearizable(b"hello".to_vec()).await.unwrap();

    println!("{}", String::from_utf8_lossy(&value.unwrap()));
    engine.stop().await.unwrap();
}`;
---

<Base
  title="d-engine: Raft consensus, embedded in your app"
  description="Fault-tolerant replication as a library. d-engine is an embeddable Raft consensus engine for Rust: strong-consistency KV, watch and leader election inside your process."
>
  <main>
    <section class="hero wrap">
      <h1>Raft consensus,<br />embedded in your app.</h1>
      <p class="sub">Fault-tolerant replication as a library. No separate cluster to run.</p>
      <p class="analogy">Think SQLite, but for keeping several servers in agreement. Consensus and replication only. Not a database.</p>
      <div class="cta">
        <code class="install">cargo add d-engine</code>
        <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/deventlab/d-engine">View on GitHub</a>
      </div>
      <p class="note">Not on Rust? Run it as a standalone service over gRPC.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap">
      <h2>One process instead of another cluster</h2>
      <div class="compare">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Typical: external coordination service</h3>
          <div class="flow">
            <span class="box">Your app</span><span class="arrow">→ network →</span>
            <span class="box dashed">etcd / ZooKeeper cluster</span>
          </div>
          <p>Deploy it. Operate it. Monitor it. Upgrade it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card primary">
          <h3>d-engine: embedded</h3>
          <div class="flow">
            <span class="box solid">Your app<small>+ d-engine</small></span>
          </div>
          <p>One process. One binary. Calls are in-process.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap">
      <h2>Kill one node. The other two keep serving.</h2>
      <img class="gif" src="/demo.gif" alt="A 3-node d-engine cluster keeps serving after one node is killed" />
    </section>

    <section class="wrap">
      <h2>Is it for you?</h2>
      <div class="compare">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Use it if</h3>
          <p>You want leader election, replication, service discovery or configuration consistency inside your own service, without running another cluster.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Build on it if</h3>
          <p>You need a specific database or state machine that is replicated and fault-tolerant. d-engine provides consensus and replication; you plug in the storage. d-lmdb is a distributed LMDB built this way.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <table class="plain">
        <thead><tr><th>Language</th><th>Embedded (in-process)</th><th>Standalone (gRPC)</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Rust</td><td>Available</td><td>Available</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Go, Java, Python, ...</td><td>Planned (C ABI)</td><td>Available</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap">
      <h2>Hello World</h2>
      <pre class="code"><code>{hello}</code></pre>
      <p>
        Scale to 3 nodes:{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/deventlab/d-engine/tree/main/examples/three-nodes-embedded">three-nodes-embedded example</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="note">Running this in production? Talk to us → <a href="mailto:contact@deventlab.com">contact@deventlab.com</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap" id="performance">
      <h2>Performance, measured against etcd</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Embedded mode, 100 requests in flight, 256 B values. AWS us-east-1, 3 × c5.2xlarge, gp3 disk.
        d-engine against etcd v3.7.2 on the same instance shape. Every acknowledged write is synced to disk first, as in etcd.
      </p>
      <div class="bench">
        <table class="plain">
          <thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>etcd (ops/s)</th><th>d-engine (ops/s)</th><th>d-engine ÷ etcd</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {embedded.map((r) => (
              <tr>
                <td>{r.label}</td>
                <td>{fmt(r.etcd)}</td>
                <td>{fmt(r.dengine)}</td>
                <td class={ratio(r) >= 1 ? "win" : "behind"}>{ratio(r).toFixed(2)}×</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="note">
        d-engine lets you swap the storage engine, and different engines perform differently. These numbers use the raft-engine log store.
        Embedded calls skip serialization and the network, so the read ratios measure that, not only the engine.
        Three rounds per case on different instances of the same shape; treat ratios as indicative, about ±20%.
        Standalone (gRPC) results and other storage engines are in the{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/deventlab/d-engine/tree/main/benches/reports">full report</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap" id="correctness">
      <h2>Correctness</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Tested with Jepsen: 5 workloads and a 6-hour soak under combined kill, partition and pause faults.
        Every commit waits for a physical fdatasync before it is acknowledged.{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/deventlab/d-engine-jepsen/blob/main/GUARANTEES.md">Read the guarantees</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap">
      <h2>Built on d-engine</h2>
      <div class="compare">
        <div class="card"><h3>d-lmdb <small>Experimental</small></h3><p>A distributed LMDB built on d-engine. <a href="https://blog.deventlab.com">Read the post</a>.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  section { padding-top: 72px; }
  .hero { padding-top: 88px; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 4rem); line-height: 1.08; margin: 0 0 20px; color: var(--dl-primary); letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.7rem; margin: 0 0 24px; color: var(--dl-primary); letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  h3 { margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  h3 small { margin-left: 8px; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--dl-muted); }
  .sub { font-size: 1.35rem; margin: 0 0 8px; }
  .analogy, .lead { color: var(--dl-muted); max-width: 720px; }
  .cta { display: flex; gap: 14px; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 28px; }
  .install { background: var(--dl-primary); color: #fff; padding: 12px 18px; border-radius: 10px; font-size: 1rem; }
  .btn { background: var(--dl-accent); color: #fff; padding: 12px 20px; border-radius: 10px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; }
  .btn:hover { filter: brightness(0.92); }
  .note { color: var(--dl-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; max-width: 760px; }

  .compare { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; }
  .card { background: var(--dl-white); border: 1px solid var(--dl-border); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px; }
  .card.primary { border-color: var(--dl-primary); }
  .card p { margin: 12px 0 0; color: var(--dl-muted); }
  .flow { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; min-height: 64px; }
  .arrow { color: var(--dl-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .box { display: inline-flex; flex-direction: column; padding: 12px 16px; border-radius: 10px; border: 1px solid var(--dl-border); background: var(--dl-ground); font-weight: 600; }
  .box small { font-weight: 500; opacity: 0.85; }
  .box.dashed { border-style: dashed; }
  .box.solid { background: var(--dl-primary); color: #fff; border-color: var(--dl-primary); }

  .gif { width: 100%; max-width: 860px; border-radius: 14px; border: 1px solid var(--dl-border); display: block; }
  .code { background: var(--dl-primary); color: #e6ebf5; padding: 24px; border-radius: 14px; overflow-x: auto; font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0 0 16px; }

  .plain { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; background: var(--dl-white); border: 1px solid var(--dl-border); border-radius: 10px; margin-top: 20px; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .plain th, .plain td { text-align: left; padding: 12px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--dl-border); }
  .plain th { color: var(--dl-muted); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .plain td:not(:first-child), .plain th:not(:first-child) { white-space: nowrap; }
  .bench { margin-top: 28px; }
  .win { color: var(--dl-primary); font-weight: 700; }
  .behind { color: var(--dl-ink); font-weight: 700; opacity: 0.7; }
</style>
